    "q-103219": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103219",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nI. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=2n\\pi $\n\nII. The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\nIII. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,0].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255329/assets/04f13f2dec860874174f51990f4260615e7be893a6be5f86b3b13857c4e8953f.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=\\pi \\pm 2\\pi ,\\pi \\pm 4\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=\\pi +2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
