    "q-70671": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70671",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$ for some $x$, then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-10\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2},$ then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-10\\pi )=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
